\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Distribution of common garden sites along a natural aridity gradient from Texas to Louisiana, US for (A) \emph  {Agrostis hyemalis} (AGHY), (B) \emph  {Elymus virginicus} (ELVI), and (C) \emph  {Poa autumnalis} (POAU). Climate data in A–C are based on 30-year normals of climate predictions (1993–2023) from PRISM data (TOM:You'll need to cite prism.), which illustrate the precipitation gradient across sites (scale on the right is in mm (TOM:This should be shown in the figure)). Red dots indicate the locations of source populations, while grey dots represent Global Biodiversity Information Facility (GBIF) occurrence records for each species within the study area.(TOM:provide citation or url for GBIF) D) Cumulative precipitation measured during the study period (MONTH 2023 - MONTH 2025) at each site, ordered west to east (TOM: I would order the bars west to east. When you say ``measured'' is this actually PRISM data?).}}{7}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
